[%think 2849] [%out 3048] [%in 2] [%cacheread 0] [%cachewrite 1748] Black is
lost in the long run. I have one rook against White's two, with five pawns
against four. White's rooks on c2 and c1 hit c6 twice. My rook on c8 defends it
only once, so the pawn can't be held. If White takes on c6 and I recapture with
the rook, I lose the rook too. I also have no escape square behind my king.
Once my rook leaves the eighth rank, Rc8+ is mate. So first I make luft with
h6. After Rxc6 I'll move the rook somewhere active, such as b8 heading for b2,
and play for as much resistance as possible. } 29. Rxc6 Rb8 { [%emt 0:00:28]
